SUMMARY:Summit Saturday: Red Hill
DESCRIPTION:If you have previously completed the Intermediate Hiking for Fitness Program or can hike 6.5 miles with at least 1\,600ft of elevation\, this hike may be right for you. We strongly recommend completion of the shorter version of the Bald Mt. hike (in and out via Bald Mountain Trail) as a pre-requisite. \nThis hike will take place (mostly) at Sugarloaf’s McCormick Addition\, starting at the Los Alamos Rd entrance to Hood Mountain Regional Park. From the Los Alamos parking lot\, we will start out on Hood Mtn Rd and cross into Sugarloaf at Salt Creek. We will take Quercus\, Headwaters\, and Grandmother Oak Trails to Red Hill. From there\, we will follow a game trail to return to Maple Glen Trail where we will have lunch. We return via Maple Glen to Headwaters Trail and backtrack to the parking lot. \nThis event requires advance registration; day-of on site tickets will not be available. There is a $10 deposit per ticket\, which will be returned post-hike\, unless you choose to donate it to support Sugarloaf. Wear appropriate footwear for rocky/slippery trails and multiple layers. Be prepared for two slippery water crossings; we strongly recommend bringing water shoes\, hiking poles\, and an additional pair of socks. Bring your lunch\, at least two quarts of water\, and sun protection. Heavy rains cancel. The Regional Park parking fee ($8 daily) applies.
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/summit-saturday-red-hill/
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, 2605 Adobe Canyon Rd\, Kenwood\, CA
CATEGORIES:Recreation
GEO:38.4427;-122.533
X-APPLE-STRUCTURED-LOCATION;VALUE=URI;X-ADDRESS=Sugarloaf Ridge State Park 2605 Adobe Canyon Rd Kenwood CA;X-APPLE-RADIUS=500;X-TITLE=2605 Adobe Canyon Rd:geo:-122.533,38.4427
END:VEVENT
